<title>UK: RESEARCH ALERT-Utd Assurance cut at Lehman.</title>
<headline>RESEARCH ALERT-Utd Assurance cut at Lehman.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1997-06-10</dateline>
<text>
<p>United Assurance Group Plc was cut to &quot;underperform&quot; from &quot;neutral&quot; at Lehman Brothers, a research note from the investment bank said on Tuesday.</p>
<p>Analysts at Lehman said there was a risk of prolonged disruption following the merger of United Friendly and Refuge which created United Assurance last October and predicted a &quot;prolonged period of new business contraction&quot;.</p>
<p>They set a price target of 420p on the stock, which was down 1/2p at 469-1/2 by 0736 GMT.</p>
<p>-- David Holmes, London Newsroom +44 171 542 4367</p>
